-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.4 (2026-11-03)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Mask the engine's top-level failure drop-in by name beside each of our five
    service drop-ins, including the xfs_healer template: one record and notice
    per failure, with the existing diagnostic and Repair
  * Keep the service start-up fixes and generic failure reporting for other units
  * Correct the documentation and regression checks: emptying OnFailure alone
    does not remove the engine's top-level handler

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.3 (2026-11-02)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 350 (Daniel, 2026-11-02: "Why machinery to keep a failure for each?"): the problems are kept by
    the edition's one engine, sparky-stereo-problems, and shown by its session notifier; the package's own
    store, notifier and user units go. status and repair keep working through the engine; dismiss is the
    engine's Hide (yours, no administrator needed, back when the problem changes); notify starts the
    session's notifier. Each drop-in empties OnFailure= before naming its own handler, so a failure of these
    units is told once, with what this package knows of it, instead of the engine's generic handler. The
    messages, word for word, are built into journal catalogs; the problems go when the package is removed
  * Nothing fails silently (ORDER 346c; Daniel, 2026-11-01: "either it works or not and the user must know"):
    each drop-in names sparky-stereo-service-problem@ in OnFailure=, so a service that cannot start is said in the
    system's language and kept in /var/lib/sparky-stereo-service-defaults/problems with its own last lines;
    the session shows it as a notification; sparky-stereo-service-defaults status, repair and dismiss
  * snmptt: no longer skipped without Net::IP; the edition's snmptt 1.5-3+sparky1 depends on libnet-ip-perl
    (Breaks: snmptt << 1.5-3+sparky1~), and a failure says what is missing
  * pkcs11-daemon: no longer skipped without its library; the edition's pkcs11-daemon 0.4.1-5+sparky1 depends on
    libsofthsm2, the library its default names (Breaks: pkcs11-daemon << 0.4.1-5+sparky1~); a library that cannot be
    loaded is said with where PKCS11_LIB is set
  * urfkill: no longer skipped behind a ConsoleKit condition; Debian's 0.5.0-8, built for ConsoleKit, fails and that is
    said with the reason (radio switches work without it)
  * xfs_healer@: xfsprogs' own --supported check again, now that it skips a file system that is not XFS (upstream
    fde1eee, carried in xfsprogs 7.2.0-1+sparky1; Breaks: xfsprogs << 7.2.0-1+sparky1~); our findmnt check, which took
    a failed findmnt for "not XFS", is gone
  * ipwatchd: a failed address probe is no longer "no address": it is said and kept, and the unit fails; no address is
    still a skip; NetworkManager's dispatcher says a check or start that fails
  * Messages in en, pl, pt_BR, fr, de, ja, ko, zh_CN and zh_TW
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ipwatchd: skipped at boot while no interface has an IPv4 address (it stopped with "No interfaces discovered"), started by NetworkManager when one comes up
  * snmptt: skipped until the Perl module Net::IP is installed, which its default ipv6_enable = 1 needs, unless IPv6 is turned off in snmptt.ini

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-15)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The APTus upgrade checker's autostart: status 1 of its normal cases (live system, no connection) counts as success

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-15)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Working defaults for services that failed at every boot: pkcs11-daemon, stas-config@, urfkill, xfs_healer@, akonadi_control, the sparky-welcome autostart
